      "type": "other",
      "url": "https://openalex.org/works/W4390095984",
      "abstract": "Methane is either captured as natural gas from natural reservoirs or might be obtained via the hydrogenation of carbon dioxide. This reaction might be pursued as a chemical reaction (Chemical Sabatier) or methanogenic bacteria (biochemical Sabatier). The methanation of carbon dioxide is gaining attention as a potential energy storage technology since abundant green power can be converted into hydrogen and then the energy can be saved in the form of methane in existing gas grids. The advantages and disadvantages of the chemical and the biochemical Sabatier are discussed.",
